Muse License
Version 1.0, 11 November 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 wahidalways. All rights reserved.

Muse is free for everyone to use. This license explains what you may do with
Muse, what needs permission first, and the rules that protect you and the
author. It is written in plain English on purpose.


1. Words used in this license

"Muse" means the Muse app and everything in this repository
(https://github.com/wahidalways/Muse): its source code, design, text,
graphics, sounds, name and icons.

"The author" means wahidalways, who owns Muse.

"You" means anyone who gets, uses or reads Muse, and any company or group
you act for.

"The official APK" means an APK published on this repository's Releases page
(https://github.com/wahidalways/Muse/releases).

"A changed version" means anything made by changing, adding to, removing
from, translating or repackaging Muse, other than the build settings allowed
in section 2.4.

"Written permission" means a message from the author that clearly gives
permission, such as a reply from the wahidalways account on GitHub.
Permission covers only what it says.


2. What you may do, for free

2.1 Use. Install and use Muse on any number of devices, for any purpose.
    This includes businesses, schools and other organizations, and their
    work devices.

2.2 Share person to person. Give the official APK, unchanged and for free,
    directly to people you know, for example by sending them the file.

2.3 Read and learn. Read the source code to learn how Muse works.

2.4 Build and change it for yourself. Build Muse from this source code, and
    change it, for your own private use. Changing only build settings, such
    as the Expo account, is fine. Keep changed code private: on your own
    devices or in a private repository.

2.5 Talk about Muse. Use the Muse name and icon to refer to Muse, for
    example in reviews, articles, videos, tutorials and links to the
    official page, as long as you do not suggest that the author made,
    approved or supports your work.


3. What needs written permission first

Unless the author gives you written permission, you may not:

3.1 Share or publish a changed version of Muse in any form. This includes a
    public fork with changes and an APK built from changed code.

3.2 Upload or offer Muse, even unchanged, on any website, app store,
    file-sharing service or other public place, other than this repository.

3.3 Sell Muse, charge money for it or for access to it, add ads to it,
    collect payments through it, or include it in anything you sell, such
    as phones sold with Muse already installed.

3.4 Copy any part of Muse's code, design, text or graphics into another
    app, website or project.

3.5 Use the Muse name or icon for another app or product, for a changed
    version, or in any way that could make people think something is
    official Muse.

3.6 Use Muse's code, design or other content to train, fine-tune or test an
    AI or machine-learning model, or to build a dataset for one.

3.7 Remove or change this license, or the copyright notice above, in any
    copy of Muse's source code.


4. Asking for permission

To ask, open an issue at https://github.com/wahidalways/Muse/issues and
explain what you want to do. The author may say yes, say no, or set
conditions such as credit or payment. No answer means no permission.


5. Bug reports, ideas and outside code

Bug reports and ideas are welcome as GitHub issues. If you share an idea or
other feedback, the author may use it freely, without owing you anything.
Muse does not take outside code, so pull requests may be closed without
review.


6. GitHub

GitHub's terms let anyone view and fork this repository on GitHub, and this
license does not take that away. A fork may be kept as it is or for your own
use, but publishing changes in it, or releasing builds from it, is covered
by section 3.


7. Open-source parts

Muse is built with open-source libraries, such as React Native and Expo.
Each library keeps its own license, and that license, not this one, covers
the library. This license gives you no rights in those libraries beyond what
their own licenses give.


8. Fair use

Nothing in this license limits what the law already lets you do without
permission, such as fair use or fair dealing. For example, you may quote a
short part of the code in a review or a lesson.


9. No warranty

Muse is provided "as is" and "as available", without any warranty, express
or implied. This includes any warranty that it is fit for a particular
purpose, works without errors, or keeps your data safe. You use Muse at your
own risk, so keep your own backups of your music and of Muse's data.


10. Limit of liability

As far as the law allows, the author is not liable for any loss or damage
that comes from using Muse, or from not being able to use it. This includes
lost data, lost music files, harm to devices and lost profits, whatever the
legal reason for the claim. Some places do not allow these limits, so they
apply only as far as the law where you live allows.


11. When your rights end

If you break this license, your rights under it end automatically. If it is
the first time, and you fully stop within 30 days after the author tells you
about it, your rights come back as if they had never ended. Sections 9, 10,
12 and 14 still apply after your rights end.


12. Law and courts

This license is governed by the laws of Bangladesh, and the courts of
Bangladesh decide any dispute about it, except where the law where you live
gives you, as a consumer, the right to use your own courts.


13. New versions of this license

The author may publish new versions of this license for future releases of
Muse. Each release is covered by the license in this repository when that
release came out. A new version never takes away rights you already had for
an older release.


14. Other terms

This license, together with any written permission from the author, is the
whole agreement about Muse. If a court finds part of it unenforceable, the
rest stays in force, and that part applies as far as it can. If the author
does not act on a breach right away, the author can still act on it later.
All rights not given in this license are kept by the author.
